      "writtenOn": "2021-11-10T16:54:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeh. We do have version of registerReceiver that can pass the handler.\n\nSince the receiver carefully post the real work to handler (with msg EVENT_CARRIER_CONFIG_CHANGED) when receive the broadcast intent, it should be no problem to let main thread handle the broadcast intent.\n\nActually it is a little tricky to pass handler here. We have to pass \"this\" object (SignalStrengthController extends Handler). But since we are in constructor, \"this\" is not ready yet. We have to re-org the logic (move the receiver out of constructor). This extra work looks like not worthy at this moment.",
